[1.] One line summary of the problem:
Bluetooth and WIFI always turned ON, on Clevo laptop (P150EM)

[2.] Full description of the problem/report:
Bluetooth and WIFI are always turned ON, on Clevo laptop (P150EM)
Bluetooth and WIFI can't be turned OFF using the FN+F11 and FN+F12 keys.
This has worked till kernel 3.6 and is broken since kernel 3.7-rc1
(and still is broken in kernel 3.8).
Bluetooth turns on right when the kernel starts booting after grub and
always stays on (FN+F12 has no effect).
When I push FN+F11 (to toggle Wifi) the LED turns off for less than a
second and the Wifi-connection get disconnected. But then the LED
comes right back ON and the Wifi gets reconnected.
See https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/linux/+bug/1131976

[3.] Keywords:
hotkeys, bluethooth, wifi, acpi, kernel-bug-exists-upstream-v3.8

